      "side": 1,
      "message": "Usually we disable LRU cache when we isolate pages for migration. So, here IIUC you do that because alloc_contig_range() might require migration? Could that regress performance in cases when alloc_contig_range() did not require migration?\n\nAlthough looking at the code, it seems __alloc_contig_migrate_range() always calls lru_cache_disable(), so maybe this is not an issue?",
